  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "During the 2026 APEC Summit, President Prabowo Subianto championed a vision of inclusive economic prosperity driven by collaborative innovation and market transparency. APEC economic leaders collectively solidified commitments to enhance economic integration and strengthen anti-corruption measures. Beyond the summit's core focus, Indonesia leveraged regional platforms to advocate for improved management of peatlands and the prevention of transboundary haze through cooperation with ASEAN and Western Pacific nations. These diplomatic efforts follow significant bilateral business agreements recently finalized between Indonesia and China, involving strategic investments valued at over 1,300 trillion rupiah. The President's call for fair competition and open partnership serves as a central pillar of Indonesia's current foreign economic policy, aiming to secure sustainable development through regional integration and strategic investment frameworks.",
